"""
hmi_live.py  -  laptop window for LIVE mode: picture files or a CAMERA (P5)

Run from the repository root: python apps/board_hmi/hmi_live.py
Needs: pip install pyserial pillow opencv-python      (tkinter comes with Python)
       (opencv-python is only needed for a real webcam; "Demo camera" works without it)
Keep tsr_link.py and the "logos" folder in the same folder as this file.
The window opens maximized and everything grows with it (a small window is just cropped).

How to use:
  LIVE mode (UART always uses live RAM on top_basys3):
    1. Choose the COM port (or "Demo (no board)") and press Connect.
    2. Choose the mode at the top.
    PICTURE FILE mode:
       "Open picture..." -> choose a cropped sign or set ROI and apply image options.
       "Send to board" for one picture, or "Send N times" to measure speed.
    CAMERA mode:
       a. Choose the camera and press "Start camera". The green square in the preview is the part
          of the picture that is sent (change its size with "Crop square"). Hold the sign inside it.
       b. Press "Start sending": the newest camera picture is sent again and again.
          The small picture in the corner of the preview is the 16 x 16 gray picture the board gets.
    3. Statistics on the right update after every answer.
       Resource and power numbers come from Vivado: type them in the boxes (they are saved).

  Speed limit of the cable: one picture = 259 bytes sent + 32 bytes answer = 291 bytes.
  UART 115200 baud, 8N1 = 10 bits per byte = 11520 bytes per second  ->  11520 / 291 = 39.6 pictures per second.
  A normal webcam gives 30 pictures per second, so the real speed is about 30 FPS or a little less.
"""
